api_surface:
Proposed API (TypeScript signatures) as part of @redwood/inference-sdk/streams:

export function fromReadableStream<T>(rs: ReadableStream<T>, opts?: { signal?: AbortSignal }): AsyncIterable<T>;

export function toReadableStream<T>(iter: AsyncIterable<T>, opts?: { highWaterMark?: number, cancel?: (reason?: any) => void }): ReadableStream<T>;

export function mapAsync<T, U>(iter: AsyncIterable<T>, fn: (item: T) => Promise<U> | U): AsyncIterable<U>;
export function filter<T>(iter: AsyncIterable<T>, predicate: (item: T) => Promise<boolean> | boolean): AsyncIterable<T>;
export function batchByCount<T>(iter: AsyncIterable<T>, n: number): AsyncIterable<T[]>;
export function batchByTime<T>(iter: AsyncIterable<T>, ms: number): AsyncIterable<T[]>;
export function throttle<T>(iter: AsyncIterable<T>, perMs: number): AsyncIterable<T>;

Example usage: (consumer wants a ReadableStream for browser APIs)

const sourceAsync = mapAsync(fromReadableStream(remoteRs), async chunk => transform(chunk));
const readStream = toReadableStream(sourceAsync, { highWaterMark: 2 });

Example retry wrapper sketch:

async function* retryable(factory, opts) {
  let attempt = 0;
  while (attempt <= opts.maxRetries) {
    try {
      for await (const x of factory()) {
        yield x;
      }
      return;
    } catch (e) {
      attempt++;
      if (attempt > opts.maxRetries) throw e;
      await wait(exponentialBackoff(attempt, opts.backoffMs));
    }
  }
}

The full surface will be exported and documented in the SDK README.
